invariant: INV-41
file: srv_auth.c
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh rsa-ifma-callers
reason: ch_srv_check verifies the RSA identity's signature under 0 in
  place of the configuration's ch_cfg.cpu, so the check never runs the
  AVX-512 IFMA path a session under the same value runs, and a value that
  names instructions the CPU lacks no longer faults at boot. The verdict
  is the same. test/tcp_blocking_loop_ifma.h requires one call to
  rsa_ifma_public from the check under a value with CH_CPU_AVX512_IFMA.
  Only an x86-64 object makes the call, so test/aes-runtime-qemu.sh builds
  bin/tcp_blocking_loop_host for x86-64 and runs it under qemu-x86_64. The
  lane skips without docker, and this then reports unguarded rather than
  caught.

--- old
    if (!verify_digest(CH_CFG_CPU(*cfg), id, sigalg, digest, sig, sig_len)) {
--- new
    if (!verify_digest(0U, id, sigalg, digest, sig, sig_len)) {
